      "message": "Give the first hour a page of its own, and ask everyone once\n\nFollowing an invitation used to drop a person on Settings under a\nbanner, with a name they could not change. Now every sign-in of\nsomebody the page has never had its say to lands on /welcome: three\nsteps, each skippable, using the whole page. Who they are (the mark\nthey choose among the drawings, the name they are shown by, a line, a\ntime zone the browser guesses first, pronouns, a link). How they sign\nin next time (a passkey where the forge can register one, a password\neither way; a new password keeps them on the page, on a fresh\nsession). What brought them here (agents, code, the organisation that\ninvited them, or just looking), which is a list of doors and records\nnothing but that the page has asked. The door, or skipping to their\nown page, is what marks it asked; from then on a sign-in goes Home.\nAccounts that existed before the page did are asked too, the first\ntime, since nobody has said who they are yet.\n\nEvery way in goes through the same rule: the sign-in form, a pasted\ntoken, a sign-in link, a passkey, a provider, and the dev identity.\nThe Settings banner for a first sign-in goes, and the walk in the\ninvitation test follows the new page.\n\nChange-Id: Iwelcome0162\nTask: t-4nzrk68jbfw73ge5qrkp47p7bm\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
